# Chapter 3 Promotion System of Saemaul Undong

First, it comprehensively coordinates the long-term, mid-term, and annual plans of Saemaul Undong;
Second, it comprehensively coordinates Saemaul Undong systematically and efficiently;
Third, it comprehensively coordinates enlightenment and public relations activities concerning Saemaul Undong.
Fourth, its function is to integrate and coordinate Saemaul education and the publication of its educational materials.
Finally, although its functions are defined as other necessary matters regarding Saemaul Undong, it maintains guidelines to review and analyze the status of Saemaul project promotion quarterly and comprehensively coordinate policies. It also established a guideline to resolve difficulties by consulting on them, having mayors and provincial governors attend the Central Council in rotation.
Meanwhile, the Saemaul Undong Central Working Committee within the Saemaul Undong Central Council performs its functions by consulting on the following matters:
First, prior consultation on matters requiring deliberation by the Saemaul Undong Central Council;
Second, working-level consultation matters between ministries regarding Saemaul Undong;
Third, consultation and review of difficulties and solutions in the promotion of Saemaul projects;
Fourth, matters concerning quarterly performance of Saemaul Undong.

### B. Composition and Functions of Provincial and Municipal Councils

#### (1) Composition

The Provincial and Municipal Councils are bodies that consult on and coordinate guidance and support for Saemaul Undong within provinces and municipalities. They are composed of the mayor or provincial governor as chairperson, and members including the vice mayor, vice provincial governor, superintendent of education, director of the Provincial Office of Rural Development, director of the Regional Construction Office, director of the Regional Communications Office, director of the regional broadcasting station, university professors, principals of agricultural high schools, branch managers of the agricultural cooperative, branch managers of the fisheries cooperative, branch managers of the forestry cooperative union, branch heads of the local veterans association, and branch managers of the Korea Electric Power Corporation.
Several characteristics can be pointed out regarding the composition of the Provincial and Municipal Councils, but first, it is notable that the organic cooperation system among related agencies was strengthened following the promotion of Saemaul projects. For instance, because the Provincial and Municipal Councils operate on the principle of a functional division of responsibilities, the director of the Provincial Office of Rural Development is in charge of Saemaul production projects, the director of the regional broadcasting station handles public relations activities for Saemaul Undong, the director of the Regional Construction Office manages national land management, and the superintendent of education oversees tasks related to Saemaul education.
